# Build output
target/
agent/Cargo.lock
kb/Cargo.lock
scratch/Cargo.lock

# Scratch is skeletal-only in git (owner's rule, the cmd pattern):
# the skeleton was committed once, then these dirs are ignored wholesale
# so normal use — transient code, skills, experiments — never lands in a
# commit. tools/overlay.sh additionally marks the tracked skeleton files
# skip-worktree so even their runtime mutations go untracked.
/data/scratch/
/scratch/

# The brain is instance-owned (docs/one-memory-cycle.md A4): nothing under
# data/kb is tracked (bdc31ba untracked the A4 freeze) and everything is
# ignored wholesale, so live deposits never dirty the tree. A fresh clone
# gets its brain from the primer (tools/setup.sh step 9). The living, reviewable
# channels are docs/kb-seed.json (the primer, refreshed only by a
# deliberate seed_export) and the subject libraries' shipped manuals
# (via agent-archivist-promote).
/data/kb/

# Local runtime values never ride the repo
/runtime/
__pycache__/
